<title>BELGIUM: USDA official attacks EU grain export subsidies.</title>
<headline>USDA official attacks EU grain export subsidies.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Department of Agriculture General Sales Manager Chris Goldthwait criticised European Union grain export subsidies during two days of talks with the European Commission, U.S. officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't understand why they continue to subsidies exports when they are the only player in the market,&quot; one U.S. official said, referring to subsidised 1996/97 sales.</p>
<p>&quot;Every time they subsidise exports they put more political pressure on the U.S. to resume the EEP (Export Enhancement Programme),&quot; the official added. &quot;They must be made aware of the consequences.&quot;</p>
<p>Goldthwait, who had talks with European Commission cereals director Jose Manuel Silva, also discussed the EU's food aid programme before leaving Brussels on Thursday.</p>
<p>U.S. officials said that meat inspection rules were not on the agenda.</p>
<p>-Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
